    "body": "This is a bit odd, because the LSU normally deals with the D$ whereas PREFETCH.I is for the I$. How does PREFETCH.I actually work today even without CHERI in such a high-performance design? I kind of suspect, as you get high-performance enough, you want a hardware prefetcher to do everything, in part because you don't want to wait for the many cycles it takes between fetching and being able to execute the PREFETCH.I, during which time you're probably hitting the instructions you were trying to prefetch?",
