    "body": "So, it's true that it's not architecturally visible whether you're executing whatever unauthorised prefetches are happening or whether you're just happening to choose to prefetch matching lines, and therefore any authorisation requirements are non-normative (until you get into side-channel microarchitectural requirement specs like Zkt), but I think the justification given here is a bit odd.",
