      "subscriptions_url": "https://api.github.com/users/jrtc27/subscriptions",
      "organizations_url": "https://api.github.com/users/jrtc27/orgs",
      "repos_url": "https://api.github.com/users/jrtc27/repos",
      "events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/jrtc27/events{/privacy}",
      "received_events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/jrtc27/received_events",
      "type": "User",
      "user_view_type": "public",
      "site_admin": false
    },
    "body": "So, I think the concerns about having PCC in the LSU are overblown, since you're already happy to feed PCC down the pipeline for AUIPCC in capability mode, and you're happy to feed DDC alongside the address for integer mode memory accesses, so the the logical thing would be to shove PCC where DDC normally goes and be done with it. I think the only real reason to not _require_ it is because, without any side-channel-specific extensions, microarchitecture is not architecture for RISC-V, and therefore you can prefetch anything you want at any point for any reason. So I would just drop the justification entirely, and for all the PREFETCH.x you have a strong recommendation that microarchitecture use DCC/PCC as appropriate to authorise the request, but that any such requirements belong in an extension pertaining to side-channel resistance.",
    "created_at": "2026-02-11T19:33:09Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-02-11T19:33:09Z",
    "html_url": "https://github.com/riscv/riscv-cheri/pull/900#discussion_r2795103404",
