    "body": "The statement\n\n> If the checks above pass, an implementation may opt to cache a copy of the cache block in a cache accessed by an instruction fetch in order to improve memory access latency, but this behavior is not required.\n\napplies equally here, without all these caveats. Such statements say nothing about what happens if the checks *don't* pass. A conforming implementation can still cache that block. It just probably shouldn't.",
